# What the image builds do not need.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so everything here is shipped to the builder
# unless it is listed. Excluding the heavy, regenerable directories is what keeps a build
# from uploading hundreds of megabytes to the daemon on every run.
#
# Deliberately short: an entry that excludes something a Dockerfile later needs produces a
# confusing "file not found" inside a build, and this file is not the place to be clever.

.git
.github

**/node_modules
**/target
**/bin
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/*.pyc

# Local artefacts that are not part of any image.
*.log
*.tgz
